  html: "To justify the credential of any travel agency, before finalization of the tour, the ideal way to check their previous guest’s references, who had hired that agency to arrange entire trip. Here are some of our previous guests remarks, who had revert with their views and feedback after their experience during the trip to India organized by us. Considering the privacy of the guests, we are not revealing direct contact details of them, however on request we can provide their contact details, if any of new guests wish to interact with the below guest. Please note all the comments are incorporated in our website, without any change of single word, and we obliged by their consent to use their comment and name in our website and forward to our new guests.\n<ul>\n<li>\n<h4>Culture of Maharashtra Tour</h4>\n<p>Mumbai – Pune – Aurangabad – Ajanta – Ellora – Shanisinghnapur –\nShirdi –\nNashik – Mumbai – Hometown\n<br />\n(11 Nights - 12 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Meruka Travels provided excellent service during our 2-week trip through Maharashtra. The agent was constantly in touch to see if everything was OK, and they accommodated late changes in the itinerary, and were very receptive to feedback and comments. On one occasion, they arranged for some items accidentally left behind in our last hotel to be sent to us, several hundred km away. The driver, guides and vehicle provided were generally all very good indeed - thank you, Meruka, for making our trip a very enjoyable and memorable one!\"</p>\n<h3>Ms. Siew Chi and Group<br />\n(Malaysia) </h3>\n</li>\n<li> <h4>Astonishing Karnataka Tour </h4>\n<p>Bangalore – Mysore – Nagarhole – Ooty – Coonoor – Ooty – Kodaikanal – Trichy – Hometown<br />\n(07 Nights - 08 Days)</p>\n<p>\"I had a great time during our 8 day trip to South India last week. We do wish it would have been longer but I had to go back to work. We loved our guides and our driver; the guides were very knowledgeable and went all out in helping us look for antiques and priceless second-hand Indian vinyl records. Our driver understood that we loved nature watching and we ended up going on many fun safaris and to a bird sanctuary to discover unique Indian wildlife. The accommodation was all perfect with great views and good standards of cleanliness. We definitely look forward to our next trip to India with you. Thank you, Meruka India.\"</p>\n<h3>Sumita Thiagarajan<br />\n(Singapore) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Kerala Backwater Tour </h4>\n<p>Kozhikode – Wayanad – Ooty – Coonoor – Ooty– Munnar – Alleppey – Kozhikode – Hometown <br />\n(07 Nights - 08 Days)</p>\n<p> \"My Kerala tour was awesome really perfect; my wife also felt the same. Thanks for the all arrangements, true compliment appreciated. We look forward to our next trip with you.\"</p>\n<h3>Vinay Pawar <br />\n(India) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>North and South India Religious Tour (Group of 69 Pax)</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Mathura/Vrindavan– Agra– Haridwar – Rishikesh – Delhi – Madurai – Rameshwaram – Kanyakumari – Trivandrum – Kovalam – Kumarakom – Alleppey – Cochin – Mumbai – Nashik – Shirdi – Mumbai – Hometown <br />\n(19 Nights - 20 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We all arrived safely back to our homes and everyone is still talking great things about your company. You all did an amazing job with the tour and I was really happy and quite pleased. I am surely bringing another tour in the near future. I have no hesitation to recommend friends and family to your company. Lots of people are ready to send their names for the next tour. All the best and please send my love and blessing to all your members of your company.\"</p>\n<h3>Pt. Munelal Maharaj<br />\nTour Leader\n(Trinidad &amp; Tobago) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Golden Triangle and Kerala Backwater Tour (Group of 13 Pax)</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Agra – Jaipur – Udaipur – Mumbai – Trivandrum – Kovalam – Alleppey – Kumarakom – Cochin <br />\n(15 Nights - 16 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Thanks so much for a wonderful job - you deserve a medal and hope to see you in January again. It was a 100% perfect trip Ashok - you are just brilliant at organizing it all and I thank you from the bottom of my heart\"</p>\n<h3>Jennifer Curtis Professor - Georgia Tech <br />\nSchool of Physics (Sydney, Australia)</h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Incredible South India Tour</h4>\n<p>Mumbai – Aurangabad – Ajanta – Ellora– Aurangabad – Chennai – Kanchipuram –\nMahabalipuram – Pondicherry –Chidambaram – Tanjore - Trichy– Madurai – Periyar – Alleppey –Kumarakom – Cochin – Ooty – Mysore –Shravanabelagola – Halebid – Belur – Hassan – Hospet– Hampi – Aihole/Pattadakal – Badami – Bijapur – Gulbarga – Bidar – Hyderabad – Mumbai <br />\n(23 Nights - 24 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We can consider the services provided as meeting expectations and, for some aspects, with extras that added value to the base package. In the overall, we will feel confident in recommending Meruka to friends that might ask advice for a similar tour in India.\"</p>\n<h3>Benvenuti<br />\n(Italy) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Enchanting Rajasthan Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Sikandra – Agra – Fatehpur Sikri – Jaipur – Chittourgarh – Udaipur – Jaipur – Neemrana –\nDelhi – Hometown <br />\n(08 Nights- 09 Days)</p>\n<p>\"I was delighted with your service.\"</p>\n<h3>Mr. Francis Gurry <br />\nDirector General<br />\nWorld Intellectual Property Organization (WIPO) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Glimpses of Tamil Nadu Tour</h4>\n<p>Chennai – Tirupati – Mahabalipuram – Kanchipuram – Pondicherry – Tanjore – Trichy – Madurai\n– Chennai – Hometown <br />\n(08 Nights - 09 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Many thanks for all the arrangements and we wish you a Happy New Year! We sincerely hope new year will be pleasant and satisfying. We thoroughly enjoyed the trip, and our driver Aasi was great. Overall we liked the tour very much.\"</p>\n<h3>Sergei and Nadia Popov<br />\n(France) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Wonderful Golden Triangle Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Sikandra – Agra – Fatehpur Sikri – Jaipur – Neemrana – Delhi <br />\n(06 Nights - 07 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Mr. Vijay was fantastic his driving skills were put to the test and up to standard. Overall we had a great time; I suggest that the program was great. It would be useful for guests to know there is a separate guide for the tours, the issue of tipping is difficult and advice on this would have been useful.\"</p>\n<h3>Alison McMillan <br />\n(Australia) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Enchanting Rajasthan Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Sikandra – Agra – Fatehpur Sikri – Jaipur – Pushkar – Jodhpur – Ranakpur – Udaipur – Chittourgarh – Delhi – Hometown<br />\n(10 Nights - 11 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Thank you very much for your help. We really enjoyed the few days we spent in India. We will certainly come back again to India and to you for the travel arrangements the next time we do. We will be highly recommending you to all our friends and relatives.\"</p>\n<h3>Paul Satkunarajah<br />\n(Australia) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Wonders of Kerala and Temple Tour</h4>\n<p>Mumbai – Cochin – Kumarakom – Pathanamthitta/Adoor – Alleppey – Periyar – Munnar – Cochin – Jaipur – Samode – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(09 Nights - 10 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Thank you for getting back to me. Yes of course we will use your company again. We have been invited to come to an Indian wedding but this time by our jeweller in Jaipur in two years so we will be in touch. Scott and I would like to thank you for getting the glasses sent. It looks like you had to go to a great deal of trouble. They arrived yesterday afternoon. We were going out to dinner and they were down stairs. Again thank you very much and also thanks to Vijay for finding them. Hope to be back in India within the next two years---again for a wedding. We will be in-touch.\"</p>\n<h3>Monica Duggan<br />\n(Australia) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Rajasthan Culture and Heritage Tour</h4>\n<p>Mumbai – Aurangabad – Ajanta – Ellora – Aurangabad – Udaipur – Chittourgarh – Jodhpur – Osian –Jaisalmer – Pokhran – Bikaner – Jaipur – Fatehpur Sikri – Agra – Sikandra – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(18Nights - 19 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We thoroughly commend you and your staff for a job very well done and we would highly recommend your service to others, which has already been done. We would go through your agency again for our next trip to India.\"</p>\n<h3>Brian and Christina Scholes<br />\n(Australia) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>North East Photography Tour</h4>\n<p>Guwahati – Bhalukpong – Dirang – Sela Pass – Tawang – Bomdila – Itanagar – Ziro – Daporijo – Along – Dibrugarh – Sibsagar – ChanglangshuVillage – Tuensang – Noklak – Pangsha – Mokokchung – Touphema – Kohima – Dimapur – Hometown<br />\n(21 nights - 22 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Our travel in Arunachal Pradesh has gone well, I'm happy with the organization and photo material. I want to note a guide Tieso, who helped us a lot. Give him the greetings and best wishes.\"</p>\n<h3>Yury Pustovoy<br />\n(Russia) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Glimpses of Tamil Nadu &amp; Kerala Beach Tour</h4>\n<p>Chennai – Tirupati – Mahabalipuram – Kanchipuram – Pondicherry – Tanjore – Trichy – Madurai\n– Periyar – Kovalam – Trivandrum – Chennai – Hometown <br />\n(13 Nights - 14 Days)</p>\n<p>\"First of all I would like to say that I thoroughly enjoyed my holiday and it was hassle free. I would certainly recommend your company to others. I was obviously met by the local company when I arrived in Chennai and they were most helpful and introduced me to my driver. I was also met by the local company in Madurai and Kovalam. I appreciated meeting them and was given a contact in case there were any queries. I would repeat that I was well impressed by the organisation of your company. You were always quick to respond to emails. I was just amazed at how smoothly everything went. THANK YOU!\"</p>\n<h3>Janette Ross<br />\n(United Kingdom) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Exotic Rajasthan Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Jaisalmer – Ossian – Jodhpur – Ranakpur – Udaipur – Chittourgarh – Udaipur – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(07 Nights - 08 Days)</p>\n<p>\"The tour was excellent planned and executed and we thoroughly enjoyed the 8 days thorough Jaisalmer, Jodhpur and Udaipur.\"</p>\n<h3>Durjoy Basu <br />(Singapore)</h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Taj, Pilgrimage and Heritage Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Haridwar – Rishikesh – Agra – Mathura – Agra – Orchha – Gwalior – Delhi – Hometown<br />\n(9 Nights - 10 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We were very much impressed with their service in our recent trip in Dec -Jan this year. Being originally from India, migrated in Australia 22 years back, we can say Meruka is far better than any other tourist operator. We have enjoyed the tour thoroughly. Thanks to you and your team. We look forward to take your service again.\" </p>\n<h3>Sankar - Mita Bhattacharya<br />\n(Victoria, Australia) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Karnataka Heritage and Ruins with Goa Tour</h4>\n<p>Bangalore – Somanthpur– Mysore – Halebid – Belur – Chikmaglur– Hospet / Hampi – Aihole – Pattadakal – Badami – Murudeshwar – Goa – Mumbai – Hometown<br />\n(11 Nights - 12 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We had a very good car, good driver, all the plans were carried out without no problems, our hotels were very good, we are more than satisfied. Hope to meet you in our next tour to INDIA\"</p>\n<h3>Joseph and Dalia Shalom<br />\n(Israel)</h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Ancient India with Beaches Tour</h4>\n<p>Mumbai – Nasik – Aurangabad – Sholapur – Bijapur – Pattadakal – Aihole – Hospet – Goa – Ganpatipule – Pune – Hometown<br />\n(15 Nights - 16 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We enjoyed our journey and complete tour very much. All the hotel-arrangements made by you were correct and we appreciated the upgrading in Taj Residency. As Europeans, the most interesting part is discovering the real life of your people and your country; in some hotels (Vijayshree) we met nice Indian men and women: this was very interesting and enjoyable for us. Vinod is an excellent driver, very gentle and polite and he speaks good English. If we had a most enjoyable round-trip, this is for a great part due to Vinod, our driver; we always felt safe with him in all that crazy road-traffic, which is part of India. If we ever come back to India, which we hope, we'll surely contact you again.\"</p>\n<h3>Odiel and Christine Theys<br />\n(Belgium) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Sun Temple and South India Tour</h4>\n<p>Kolkata – Bhubaneshwar – Konark – Puri – Hyderabad – Bidar – Gulbarga – Bijapur – Badami – Hospet – Hampi – Hubli – Mumbai – Kolkata – Hometown<br />\n(20 Nights - 21 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We thank you for the well-organized tour, the pickup and drop off from airports, very good drivers and cars, so also the guides. The tour was beautiful, but we are very disappointed in the restaurants and location from some hotels.\" </p>\n<h3>Willy Campos <br />\n(Netherlands)</h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>North East India Tour</h4>\n<p>Kolkata – Sunderbans – Guwahati – Kaziranga – Guwahati – Bhubaneshwar – Konark – Puri – Bhubaneshwar – Kolkata – Hometown <br />\n(16 Nights - 16 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We got back to Switzerland last week after a wonderful trip, thanks to you. I thought I will give you some feedback on the trip. I really appreciated your efficiency and immediate responses, especially when we had problems with the flight connections. Mr. JaipalRaheja in Calcutta was very accessible and helpful. All the local guides in Calcutta were also knowledgeable and friendly. I would like to make a special mention of Mr. RupakAdhikari in Assam who accompanied us during our entire stay and was extremely helpful and friendly. He really made our time in Assam memorable. All in all a very good trip - I will be in touch for any future trips we do in India.\"</p>\n<h3>Raji Sundaram<br />\n(Switzerland) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Majestic Rajasthan Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Agra – Jaipur – Pushkar – Jodhpur – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(08 Nights - 09 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We are back from our trip and I would like to thank you for organizing. Thus far, hotels have been up to the expectation and this is a truly magnificent country! I would like to make a comment regarding the driver we had. He was a very nice, polite and skillful driver.\" </p>\n<h3>Isabelle Brasier <br />\n(Hong Kong) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Duet of North &amp; South India Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Haridwar/Rishikesh – Delhi – Agra – Ranthambhore – Jaipur – Delhi – Cochin – Munnar\n– Alleppey – Kumarakom – Kovalam – Trivandrum – Mumbai – Hometown <br />\n(16 Nights - 17 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Nice to hear from you. Once again, thanks so much for all your patience and help in organizing our trip, it was by far the best holiday I’ve ever had, ever. Please give us a shout if you ever come to the UK! Having only ever travelled in Europe and the States I wanted to go somewhere a bit more adventurous to experience a totally different culture. I thought, where better than India. I didn't know where to start in terms of organizing where to go, etc so I contacted Meruka (i think i got their website address of the Indian tourist board). After that all I had to do was provide a list of things I wanted included in my itinerary and Meruka took care of the organizing! We sent a lot of emails back and forth till we were 100% satisfied with our itinerary. Tashi was so patient with us! There were 7 of us travelling together and Meruka took away all the pain of organizing the trip and also all the pain of worrying about accommodation, travel etc during the holiday. As soon as we stepped out of the airport in Delhi we were greeted by our Meruka representative and driver. Meruka took care of us from that minute till the minute we got on the plane home. I can't sing their praises enough really. The bus was spacious, comfortable and air-conditioned. The driver was ace! The itinerary was packed - we never had a dull moment. Even in the 6 hour bus rides, which sound a lot, our eyes were never bored. Our whole holiday (18days) was stress-free and fun-filled. I wasn't sure whether i was going to love or hate India after hearing different people's reports but i fell in love with the place. I've never before been anywhere more alive and vibrant and colourful. All the people have an air of calmness amongst all the chaos which just seems to work. I miss it and it will definitely not be my last time in India. If going again I would not hesitate to contact Meruka!\"</p>\n<h3>Kirsty Thomson<br />\n(United Kingdom) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Captivating Karnataka Tour</h4>\n<p>Bangalore – Mysore – Srirangapatna – Somnathpur – Belur – Halebid – Hassan – Sravanabelagola – Bangalore – Hometown<br />\n(05 Nights - 06 Days)</p>\n<p>\"I and all my friends want to thank you and your collaborators for our beautiful journey. The hotels you suggest were very nice and comfortable, our guides were qualified and very helpful and friendly, and our driver was the best I knew in all my journeys. It was all very good. I'm very satisfied of your work and I'll tell about your agency with all my friends. Thank you very much for all. I'll write to you again, if I'll want to do another tour in South India. You are a wonderful tour operator!\"</p>\n<h3>Valeria Rossi<br />\n(Italy) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Golden Triangle &amp; Pilgrimage Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Haridwar/Rishikesh – Agra – Jaipur – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(10 Nights - 11 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We had a lovely trip to India, thanks to you and your organization: my wife and I enjoyed it very much as I am sure my friends did too.\"</p>\n<h3>Stefano Livi<br />\n(Texas, USA) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Rhythm of North India and Kerala Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi - Patna – Bodhgaya - Varanasi – Khajuraho – Agra – Jaipur – Delhi – Cochin – Munnar – Periyar – Alleppey – Kumarakom - Cochin – Hometown <br />\n(14 Nights- 15 Days)</p>\n<p>\"I wanted to let you know what an amazing trip to India I had with my friend, Catherine Maas.\nAnd so much of the success of our trip I can attribute to you and your great help in organizing the places we visited and hotels we stayed in as well as the remarkable drivers, who really gave our trip that extra special plus! I am very grateful that I found you as our travel consultant and appreciate how much time you took to work out all the details and patiently make the changes that gave our trip a personal touch. Everything went very smoothly and remarkably without any real difficulty. So, please accept my deep thanks and appreciation for all that you contributed to our memorable adventure in India!\" </p>\n<h3>Judith Kneen<br />\n(Boston)</h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Exotic India Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Jabalpur – Bandhavgarh – Jabalpur – Agra – Jaipur – Delhi – Bagdogra – Glenburn – Bagdogra – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(13 Nights -14 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Just wanted to drop a line and thank you for all your help and time. We had a great time in India. The company that you worked with that met me in Delhi and provided transportation is good. The driver was a good man and not \"imposing\" which is what I like. He drove us to where we wanted to go. No interference. He only made a recommendation when we were in Agra which proved to be the highlight of visiting Agra! He recommended for us to go to the show, which was great. We enjoyed the hotels and the lodges. All were good. Site seeing was great.\" </p>\n<h3>Mohammed Attia<br />\n(Damman) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Karnataka History, Nature and Beach Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Goa – Gokarna – Jog Falls – Chikmagalur – Bhadra Wildlife Reserve – Chikmagalur / Kemmannugundi – Belur – Halebid –Hassan – Sravanabelagola – Mysore – Ranganthitu – Srirangapatna – Somnathpur – Bylakuppe – Mangalore – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(15 Nights- 16 Days)</p>\n<p>\"On the whole it was a very pleasant trip. I found that Gokarna was a place much more \"sattvic\" then others, maybe including Mysore. I hope for the future we can work out together a different scheme in organizing our trips .I want to thank you again for all your attention and your personal help in organizing and making real this fantastic trip.\"</p>\n<h3>Ferdinando Baldini<br />\n(Russia)</h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Exotic India Tour</h4>\n<p>Mumbai – Shirdi – Mumbai – Bangalore – Puttaparthi – Bangalore – Jaipur – Pushkar – Jodhpur – Ranakpur – Udaipur – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(16 Nights - 17 Days)</p>\n<p>\"With reference to my trip, it was fantastic! I was happy with all the accommodation arrangements but I liked Shradda inn the best in Shirdi more so because it was the cleanest and very peaceful esp. at night. I loved the spacious eating area and the food at Shraddha. My driver in Mumbai spoke English well. Ending my tour in Udaipur was really nice. Overall, I was very happy with your services.\"</p>\n<h3>RoshneeBhaga<br />\n(South Africa) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Maharashtra &amp; Rajasthan Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Agra – Jaipur – Bikaner – Jaisalmer – Jodhpur – Udaipur – Mumbai – Aurangabad – Mumbai – Hometown <br />\n(14 Nights – 15 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We are back home now and we are enjoying the beautiful moments we experienced during our holidays in India. We sincerely thank you once again for accommodating all our needs even during stressful time at the very beginning. A big thanks to all our drivers and guides for doing a magnificent job.\"</p>\n<h3>William and Joseph<br />\n(Australia) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Grand India Tour </h4>\n<p>Mumbai – Ahmedabad – Patan – Modhera – Udaipur – Jodhpur – Jaisalmer – Bikaner – Pushkar – Hometown <br />\n(19 Nights - 20 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Thank you for the wonderful trip we had!! everything went perfectly: Mall Singh was such a nice person (always ready to respond to all our questions , to share with us all his knowledge and he definitely took care of us ,trying to make us feel comfortable in all kind of situation) and a very good driver( which is not easy in the crazy Indian traffic). The guides also were excellent (I’ve learned so many things from art to food, from religions and tradition to medicine etc. The thing I liked the most was that guides didn't just explain us what we were seeing but also try to include us in their life contest so that we can \"act like Indian\" and not just be visitors. I've never thought I could see, learn, taste so many different things, i felt as if I were \"part\" of India and that was exactly what I was looking for! I've loved this trip so much that I’m still always talking about India, seeing Indian movies (I went to the presentation in Rome of \"My name is Khan\" with live presence of Shah Rukh Khan!), and eating Indian food. Can't wait to come back! Of course also the hotels, car, plan tickets were excellent; so I promise I will suggest your company to anyone who wants to come to India! So in conclusion thank you for having organised this magic trip!!\"</p>\n<h3>Irene Avagnina and Virginia Coradini<br />\n(Italy) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Delhi and Agra Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Agra – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(03 Nights - 04 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We've just return Beijing and just sit in front of my computer. Yes, indeed, we had a great time in India and the trip and organization was very good. Our driver, our guides are all very nice, kind and considerate.\"</p>\n<h3>Dr. Li Wuxia<br />\n(China) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Ooty, Kodaikanal and Masinagudi Tour</h4>\n<p>Goa – Madurai – Kodaikanal – Ooty –Coonor–Masinagudi– Bangalore – Goa– Hometown<br />\n(06 Nights - 07 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Thank you for arranging the tour just completed, to South India. The arrangements for flights, car and driver and accommodation were all very satisfactory and went smoothly. The driver, Babu was a very pleasant person and a good driver. The 3 places we stayed at were very good and we only have one comment to make, which is about the last resort. Jungle Hut, Masinagudi. Accommodation and food very good.Staff very helpful. Unfortunately, the arrangements for the walks, safaris and other activities dealt with by the \"Naturist\" were very vague and only\nexplained verbally by him to visitors. Anyway, thank you again, for organizing our trip as efficient as always.\" </p>\n<h3>Charmian Byrne <br />\n(Goa)</h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Exotic Rajasthan Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Mandawa – Bikaner – Jaisalmer – Jodhpur – Mount Abu – Udaipur –Pushkar – Jaipur– Agra – Khajuraho –Varanasi – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(19 Nights - 20 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We enjoyed our tour again; we saw very interesting places and took thousands of photos in addition to the thousands taken last year in the South where we were with you. The whole tour was very well organized again We think all the hotels were excellent choice, special places, like the one in Bikaner, and Mandawa. We shall long remember the wonderful places we saw in Bikaner, Jaisalmer, Mandawa, Agra, Khajuraho and at the other parts of our journey. We hope we can return to \"incredible\" India one day.\" </p>\n<h3>Judith (both of them), István, Attila, Marta <br />\n(Hungary)</h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Essence of South India Tour</h4>\n<p>Mumbai – Madurai – Trichy – Tanjore – Chidambaram – Pondicherry – Mahabalipuram\n– Kanchipuram– Chennai – Mumbai– Hometown <br />\n(08 Nights - 09 Days)</p>\n<p>Overall, the trip was superb in all ways. The tour program, transportation, accommodation and the whole arrangement were perfect. My parents and I would like to express our gratitude to your assistance throughout the trip and your patience and help in responding to my every single question in my emails to you since one month before the trip. The driver, Mr. R. Magesh is an extremely nice guy. We were impressed by his driving skills as he was able to drive us to all destinations safely and promptly no matter how difficult the road conditions were. We would definitively recommend you and your company to our friends who plan to travel to India. \"</p>\n<h3>Jason Leung<br />\n(Hong Kong) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Maharashtra, Gujarat, Rajasthan &amp; Karnataka Tour</h4>\n<p>Mumbai – Nashik – Trimbakeshwar – Aurangabad – Mumbai – Hubli – Badami – Hospet – Hampi – Bangalore – Ahmedabad – Palitana – Bhavnagar – Sasan Gir – Jamnagar – Bhuj – Nakhatrana –\nAhmedabad – Udaipur – Jodhpur – Jaisalmer – Bikaner – Jaipur – Agra – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(29 Nights - 30 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Thank you for a beautiful journey and for your kindness during our trip in India. We appreciate your kind and quick responds regarding the car replacement, the hotels (when our rooms were given to others by some of the hotels) etc. We had good drivers, and in most places very good guides (like Ishraq, Husain, Thomas Bansod) I've already recommended your travel agency to my friends. I intend to return to India which I like very much. Hopefully I'll also stay a day or two in Neemrana Fort Palace before returning home, thank you for your recommendation to visit there.\"</p>\n<h3>Rosen Shoshana <br />\n(Israel)</h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Extensive South India Tour Pro</h4>\n<p>Cochin – Alleppey – Kumarakom – Periyar – Munnar – Ooty – Mysore – Srirangapatnam –\nBangalore – Hometown <br />\n(15 Nights - 16 Days)</p>\n<p>\"At the end of the tour we could say that everything meets our expectations and even when the English of the driver was a little difficult to understand for us, he drove us save and comfortable to all our destinations, he brought us to nice restaurants during the tour where we could have typical Indian food and not only tourist food. His car was always clean and he knew where to drive. All hotels where comfortable, clean and with a good service. The tour guides we had in Periyar, Mysore and Bangalore where experienced ones with a very good English pronunciation that we could understand them perfectly. Of course you can send our contact details and email address to new guests. And when we do our next tour to India, starting in Bangalore and go north-west, we will of course choose your agency. Because travelling with Meruka is a comfortable and safe way to travel in beautiful India.\"</p>\n<h3>Matthias &amp; Ruth Frank <br />\n(Germany) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Golden Triangle Tour</h4>\n<p>Jaipur – Agra – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(04 Nights - 05 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Tashi, the feedback from the whole group, was that your guys were very professional and I would be happy to put my reference for future customers who are interested in travelling with you. Promptly picked up at each venue by driver and tour guide. Van was clean and comfortable to travel in. Some of the additional activities we visited for example visiting how carpets were made, fabric shops etc were good as the group were able to see and purchase some of the local merchandise. Strong recommendation - Chandni Chowk should be always be in the itinerary as it gives tourist a feel of village life. \"</p>\n<h3>Sean Sebastian<br />\n(Australia) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Rajasthan Forts and Palaces Tour </h4>\n<p>Delhi – Agra – Jaipur – Pushkar – Udaipur – Jodhpur – Jaisalmer – Bikaner – Mandawa – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(15 Nights - 16 Days)</p>\n<p>\"I am writing to thank you for all your efforts on my behalf organizing my recent trip round Rajasthan, all the hotels you chose were excellent, the arrangements were spot on and the itinerary was packed and extremely interesting. I would like to mention two individuals in particular; one was the guide you arranged in Jodhpur who was excellent and had a huge range of background and historical knowledge which he used to put many things in perspective without making me feel I was being lectured to. The other was my driver, Mr Ram, who was unfailingly helpful, friendly and organized, making sure I was where was supposed to be at the right time explaining where I should go as well as advising how much to pay rickshaw drivers etc.. I think it is important to remember that whoever organizes the trip and however efficiently it is done, the person who 'delivers' the service, i.e. the driver, is the person who can make or break the holiday and is very much the 'face' of Meruka.\"</p>\n<h3>Peter Bywater<br />\n(USA) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>India Pilgrimage Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Haridwar – Delhi – Agra – Ranthambhore – Jaipur – Pushkar – Jodhpur – Udaipur – Ahmedabad – Porbandar – Mumbai – Goa – Mumbai – Hometown <br />\n(24 Nights - 25 Days)</p>\n<p>\"As for the feedback the whole tour was superbly organized from Gajendra meeting us at Delhi airport to your driver dropping us to Mumbai International airport. Gajendra gave us useful info and was helpful during the tour. All the hotels were very good and some were excellent (Welcome Heritage Ranthambhore, Alsisar Haveli Jaipur, Pushkar Palace) and some were outstanding (Shikar Badi Udaipur, Lemon Tree Goa). The location of Pushkar Palace and Lemon Tree was perfect. Most of the places we visited were very good and the guides very informative especially in Agra, Fatehpur Sikri, Jaipur and Mumbai. And that was the problem with Claremont in Delhi which was too far from the centre and impossible to just go for a walk or go shopping without one to two hour car journey. The car was comfortable and the driver Nanu was always prompt, informative and very helpful throughout the tour and especially at the railway station in Ahmedabad. Most of all we would like to thank you for your patience and for organizing such a memorable tour.\"</p>\n<h3>Naresh Kana <br />\n(Canada) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Golden Triangle Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Agra – Jaipur – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(06 Nights - 07 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We had a magnificent trip. We enjoyed the sites, food, people and the weather. Everything went smoothly. The Golden triangle portion of our trip was particularly rich. We also liked our stay in Mumbai. We had very experienced drivers and guides. In particular, we liked Ramarand, our guide in Mumbai and the driver Bansidar in Golden triangle. While I would recommend Ramada Plaza for a stay in New Delhi, Alsisar hotel in Jaipur was a highlight.\"</p>\n<h3>Jagoda Pasic <br />\n(Seattle) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Unexplored North East Tour</h4>\n<p>Guwahati – Nameri – Dirang–Sela Pass – Tawang – Bomdila – Itanagar – Ziro – Daporijo – Along – Dibrugarh – Mon – Jorhat – Kohima – Silghat – Guwahati – Shillong – Cherrapunji – Guwahati –Hometown <br />\n(25 Nights - 26 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Of course we had a phantastic trip. Your organization was just perfect. We enjoyed it a lot! Highly professional both guide and driver (Teiso&amp;Burman), always good humoured, never angry, always tried their best, great team, good knowledge. \"</p>\n<h3> Sabina Rommler &amp; Andreas Lupp <br />\n(Germany) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Maharashtra Sacred Caves and Adventure Tour </h4>\n<p>Goa – Mumbai – Aurangabad – Bhandardara – Mumbai – Murud Janjira – Mumbai – Goa – Hometown <br />\n11 Nights - 12 Days)</p>\n<p>\"The trip was unforgettable, thank you once again for your irreplaceable help in consulting, advising and organizing! Of course you can give my contacts to anyone and I will warmly suggest addressing you for organizing their trip.\"</p>\n<h3>Ferdinando Baldini<br />\n(Russia) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Best of Maharashtra Tour</h4>\n<p>Mumbai – Pune – Aurangabad – Ajanta/Ellora – Pune – Hometown <br />\n(07 Nights – 07 days)</p>\n<p>\"We had a wonderful trip. The stays at Meadows, Transit and Ivy Studios were very comfortable. The breakfasts served were very good. The car was comfortable. The driver was very courteous. Only complaint is that he could not talk in English. Our tour guide Thomas in Aurangabad was very knowledgeable and very informative. We enjoyed the tours very much.\"</p>\n<h3>Rama Nathan<br />\n(USA) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Golden Triangle with Rajasthan Culture &amp; Heritage Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Agra – Jaipur – Pushkar – Bijaipur – Chittourgarh – Udaipur – Manvar – Jodhpur – Delhi –Hometown <br />\n(13 Nights - 14 Days)</p>\n<p>\"In global terms we have had an excellent trip to India, and we enjoyed so much everything. We can say we had a great experience in a wonderful land, covered by a high level logistics according to price. To share the trip with Banwari and Krishan has been a fantastic experience. traveller. We are very glad with the hotels. The service, rooms and bookings we had in all hotels has been very good, and this had been a high level service you provide us. The welcome and assistance of Mr. Gajendra Pareek has been excellent and very helpful. Always at our disposal in the distance, and very professional.Great experience also with him. Finally let me tell you we come back to Barcelona with a great experience and with wishes to visit India again soon. It has been globally a wonderful experience. Thank you very much for everything and hope to keep in touch. \"</p>\n<h3>Alex Rafart and Group <br />\n(Barcelona) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Tamil Nadu, Kerala and Karnataka Triangle Tour</h4>\n<p>Bangalore – Mysore – Ooty – Cochin – Kumarakom – Periyar – Madurai – Trichy – Tanjore – Pondicherry – Mahabalipuram – Kanchipuram – Chennai – Tirupati – Chennai – Hometown <br />\n(13 Nights - 14 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Meruka Travels was very professional, responsive and accommodating to our needs. Planning was exquisite with paperwork presented to us in a very thorough and professional manner. Tashi was incredibly resourceful and considerate in preparing our trip schedule. She made necessary changes on request with a genuine care and provided excellent feedback every time I consulted her. The driver and the car were high commendable. We had an excellent driver, Shankar, who conducted himself very professionally and treated us very well. I would recommend Meruka\nTravels, Tashi and Shankar to anyone who wishes to travel and see beautiful India. Best Regards.\" </p>\n<h3>Dr. Jana Kankesan <br />\n(Canada) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Golden Triangle Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Jaipur – Agra – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(04 Nights - 05 Days)</p>\n<p>\"I want to express my own and my companions’ satisfaction with all the arrangements made by your company for our recent tour of Rajasthan. Everything went very smoothly. In particular I wish to thank your local representative in Delhi , Mr Pareek and the Driver who was a delight to travel with ( and by the way the driver is a very good guide as well as a good driver , with good English and a great knowledge of the local heritage ) Once again thank you.\" </p>\n<h3>J.Gamble <br />\n(Bahrain) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Golden Triangle and North India, Himachal Tour</h4>\n<p>Amritsar – Dalhousie – Dharamshala – Manali – Shimla – Delhi – Agra – Ranthambhore – Jaipur – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(16 Nights - 17 Days)</p>\n<p>\"You have indeed been good ambassadors to your country. When we can afford to take another holiday in India, we will certainly be in touch.\" </p>\n<h3> Paul Carvosso <br />\n(United Kingdom) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>South India Culture and Temple Tour</h4>\n<p>Bangalore – Mysore – Ooty – Kodaikanal – Madurai – Rameshwaram – Tanjore – Trichy – Chidambaram – Pondicherry – Tiruvannamalai – Mahabalipuram – Kanchipuram – Mahabalipuram – Chennai – Hometown <br />\n(15 Nights - 16 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We want to tell you that we enjoyed our stay in India very, very much and want to say you organized our tour wonderfully. Your daughter was just like you described her in your letter, she was a sweet, very nice girl who was good companion, and particularly to the younger generation in our party. We all liked her very much. The success of the tour was also due to your choosing Mr Ramachandra to be our driver and guide, who did an excellent job in every field during the whole two-week journey. We all were greatly satisfied with his performance. We think we liked our stay in India so much, it was so interesting and pleasant that we will return some time if we can. Tashi can tell you how many photos we made which will always be reminding us of the moments of the tour.\" </p>\n<h3>Fesus Istvan<br />\n(Hungary) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Maharashtra Heritage, Culture and Goa Beaches Tour</h4>\n<p>Mumbai – Shirdi – Aurangabad – Ajanta /Ellora – Pune – Goa – Mumbai – Hometown <br />\n(13 Nights- 14 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We just got back to Rome a few hours ago and I wanted to thank you so much for all the hard work your agency did to make our trip enjoyable. Everyone was so kind and professional including the drivers Shiva and Ganesh and all the guides. We all wish you and your agency a prosperous New Year and serenity. I will certainly recommend your agency to any friends planning to travel in India. \"</p>\n<h3>Lila Di Caprio<br />\n(Rome, Italy) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Nagaland and Kaziranga National Park Tour</h4>\n<p>Kolkata – Dimapur – Khonoma – Kohima – Touphema – Wokha – Longkhum – Mockokchung – Jorhat – Majauli – Jorhat – Kaziranga – Guwahati – Kolkata – Hometown <br />\n(14 Nights - 15 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We have returned from our trip and had a great time. We loved the home stays and highly recommend them as the best way to meet and interact with people instead of hotels. The new home stay in Guwathi (John &amp;ShiantaKhating) was wonderful and they were incredibly nice people. Kevi, our guide in Nagaland was the best guide. His English was great and he was excellent. The other guides did not have great English skills, but still all was well. Jay was great in Kolkatta and was most helpful. We had an excellent trip \" </p>\n<h3>Susan Dawson <br />\n(USA) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>South India Culture and Temple Tour</h4>\n<p>Chennai – Tirupati – Chennai – Mahabalipuram – Kanchipuram – Pondicherry – Tanjore – Trichy – Madurai – Rameshwaram – Kanyakumari – Trivandrum – Kovalam – Alleppey – Kumarakom – Munnar – Ooty – Mysore – Bangalore – Hometown <br />\n(16 Nights - 17 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We had great time in south India also very nice stay and good food. Very good driver and knowledgeable. If we have to travel in India we definitely give you call for future tour in India.\"</p>\n<h3>Virendra S. J. Zala <br />\n(USA) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Enchanting Rajasthan and Mumbai Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Agra – Jaipur – Jodhpur – Manvar – Udaipur – Mumbai – Pune – Hometown <br />\n(09 Nights - 10 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We reached to hometown safely Our Rajasthan trip was very successful and went without any hitches. Thank you for the excellent arrangements\"</p>\n<h3>Sam Krishna <br />\n(Toronto) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>South India Tour</h4>\n<p>Bangalore – Mysore – Ooty – Kodaikanal – Madurai – Rameshwaram – Kanyakumari – Kovalam – Trivandrum – Tirupati – Chennai – Pondicherry – Chennai – Hometown <br />\n( 12 Nights - 13 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Thank you very much for arranging our south India tour during October/November. The ternary, the transportation, hotels arrange by you exceeded our expectation. WE loved it all. My grand children also enjoyed it very much. It was one of the best vacations we have. It was time well spend and at reasonable cost. Please convey our sincere thanks to both the drivers who were with us throughout our travel. You will be our tour operator whenever we visit India in future. Again thank you very much for all you have done for us.\"</p>\n<h3>Arvind Patel<br />\n(United Kingdom) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Exotic North India and Nepal Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Mandawa – Bikaner – Jaisalmer – Jodhpur – Udaipur – Bijaipur – Bundi – Jaipur – Agra – Gwalior – Orchha – Khajuraho – Varanasi – Kathmandu – Nagarkot – Kathmandu – Pokhra – Kathmandu– Hometown <br />\n(24 Nights - 25 Days)</p>\n<p>\"The trip was well organized and we always had appreciated the support. We had during the entire trip. In particular we are grateful that your guide in Jodhpur took care of the problem of our daughter Martina, bringing us to the hospital, taking care of the doctors and personnel there and of the medicines later. The driver in India was very good and he really was helping us a lot. Mr. Manesh was excellent and he solved many problems for us, the last one about our baggage left in Delhi that we needed to pick it up on the way back from Nepal, without a (multiple) valid visa for India. We really appreciated the organization of the trip and we will suggest your company to any friend who will plan visiting India and Nepal\" </p>\n<h3>Dr. Luigi Spinoglio<br />\n(Italy) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>South India Tour</h4>\n<p>Bangalore – Sravanbelagola – Hassan – Halebid – Belur – Mysore – Srirangapatnam – Somnathapur – Bannur – Mysore – Ooty – Metupalaiyam – Madurai – Periyar – Alleppey – Kumarakom – Cochin – Hometown <br />\n(13 Nights- 14 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Dear Mr. Pareek, Thank you. The trip was a success. No complaints. Things went on well. The coach, the driver, the helper and your representatives were extremely capable and looked after the guests very well. Your communication has always been very prompt and helpful Mr. Deena Nath, your guide is by far the best guide I have ever come across. Not only is he knowledgeable, he is very good in PR as well. I think you people should use him more often. The arrangements were very good and the hotels you chose along with the places for lunch were very very good. All in all, I would gladly recommend you to anyone interested in a trip to India. Thank you for a wonderful trip\" </p>\n<h3>MohanaSosale<br />\n(United Kingdom) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Mumbai and Kerala Backwaters Tour</h4>\n<p>Mumbai – Cochin – Periyar – Alleppey – Kumarakom – Kovalam – Trivandrum – Mumbai – Hometown <br />\n(10 Nights-11 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We have reached safely in England on Saturday 16th Sept. Apart from the couple of things I mentioned to you we had a great holiday. Already a few of my friends have inquired about your Travel Co. I will be giving them your E-mail and the website address so they would be contacting you in the near future\"</p>\n<h3> Dinesh Ravalia <br />\n(London) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Enchanting North India and Rajasthan Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Agra – Ranthambhor – Jaipur – Jodhpur – Udaipur – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(09 Nights - 10 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Thank you so very much for organizing an exciting and a truly memorable trip for us in Rajasthan, Agra and Delhi, within a very short time. We really enjoyed our stay in India, which gave us immense opportunity to learn and experience history, culture, traditions, lifestyles and many more aspects of day to day life in India/Rajasthan. Thank you so much once again for arranging a marvellous holiday for us. It was truly memorable!\"</p>\n<h3>Harshini Satharasinghe<br />\n(Sri Lanka) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>North India Goa Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Agra – Ranthambhor – Jaipur – Mumbai – Surat – Mumbai – Goa – Mumbai – Hometown <br />\n(20 Nights - 21 Days)</p>\n<p>\"The holiday was very enjoyable. We found the service from your agency and others very good, everyone was prepared to help and assist. The trip went according to the detail plan that was agreed by both of us. The hotels were in proper condition and drivers/guides were experienced. If we go back to India we will definitely use Meruka India Tourism Service again\"</p>\n<h3>Jayesh Mistry<br />\n(United Kingdom) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Vision of India Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Jaipur –Agra – Khajuraho – Varanasi – Bodhgaya – Rajgir – Nalanda – Patna – Kolkata – Mumbai – Chennai – Mahabalipuram – Kanchipuram – Pondicherry – Nagapattinam – Tanjore – Bangalore – Mysore – Bangalore – Hometown <br />\n(25 Nights - 26 Days )</p>\n<p>\"We are very satisfied with Meruka India Tourism Service for helping us in planning and organizing the 25-day trip within entire India in Jul-Aug 2006. The timings and the connections between cities which involves flights, trains and cars have been done very well\"</p>\n<h3> Teresa Yan <br />\n(Beijing) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Rajasthan Tour Plan </h4>\n<p>Delhi – Agra – Jaipur – Jodhpur – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(05 Nights - 6 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We were pleased with the service and I would like to thank you for your time and effort\"</p>\n<h3>Irene Steslow <br />\n(USA) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Mumbai, Ajanta Ellora &amp; Golden Triangle Tour</h4>\n<p>Mumbai – Aurangabad – Pune – Bangalore – Delhi – Agra – Jaipur – Delhi – Hometown<br />\n(12 Nights - 13 Days)</p>\n<p>\"As the person who organized Mrs. Atwater's vacation in India, I'd like to let you know that overall we were very satisfied with the arrangements you made for her and how closely you were able to meet our specifications for the itinerary. The cost of the package was also reasonable and the hotels chosen more than met her expectations. The only hiccup was some confusion that occurred on her return to Delhi from Agra etc. regarding where she would be picked up from but all said and done this was only a minor problem. The drivers and staff involved were also all satisfactory and many of them were excellent. My wife and I plan to tour parts of India later this year and we are strongly considering utilizing your services at that time\"</p>\n<h3>Victoria Atwater<br />\n(USA) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>North India Rajasthan Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Muzaffarnagar – Agra – Ranthambhor – Jaipur – Pushkar – Udaipur – Jodhpur – Manvar – Jaisalmer – Bikaner – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(19 Nights - 20 Days)</p>\n<p>\"I would like to say thank you for the well organised trip with your agency.Weare very happy with the services on location and especially we would point out the friendly and reliable services from our driver. We enjoyed the nice and interesting trip through India and we hope that we have an opportunity to come back to India in the nearest future.\"</p>\n<h3>Nicole Huppertz<br />\n(Frankfurt) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>South India Kerala Tour</h4>\n<p>Mumbai – Cochin – Alleppey – Kumarakom – Munnar – Periyar – Madurai – Tanjore – Pondicherry – Mahabalipuram – Kanchipuram – Chennai – Hometown <br />\n(14 Nights- 15 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Excellent services for everything, very smooth tour- All the hotels were superb, delicious food, Coach, driver and Guide was excellent. All the group members enjoyed the trip immensely. Thanks\" </p>\n<h3> Van Danilo <br />\n(Switzerland) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Rajasthan Tour Plan </h4>\n<p>Mumbai – Udaipur – Jodhpur – Jaisalmer – Manvar – Pushkar – Ranthambhor – Jaipur – Mumbai – Hometown <br />\n(12 Nights - 13 Days)</p>\n<p>\"We were very happy with your kind and professional service. This was really excellent and we had a wonderful trip thanks to your help\"</p>\n<h3>Miriam Petri <br />\n(Germany) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Rajasthan Forts and Palaces Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Mandawa – Bikaner – Nagaur – Jaisalmer – Jodhpur – Rohet – Mount Abu – Udaipur – Bundi – Pushkar – Jaipur – Agra – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n( 19 Nights - 20 Days )</p>\n<p>\"It was a really wonderful travel!!!!Rajasthan is very fantastic and Meruka service was so excellent!!!Driver was a good friend and the car was very comfortable. Palace-hotels were like in my dreams!!! My next trip in India will be surely with Meruka Tourism Service!!!!We will see soon!!!! Giorgia from Bologna\"</p>\n<h3> Giorgia Palmentieri <br />\n(Italy) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Heart of Himalayas Tour</h4>\n<p>Mumbai – Delhi – Leh – Saspol – Lamayuru – Nubra – Leh – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(10 Nights - 11 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Believe me, we had marvelous vacation and I was so glad to have gone through your company and specially you. Mr. Tushar was another wonderful person who did sort out all our loose ends. Again, Ashok thank you very much for my family and myself to have such a well-organized tour throughout India\"</p>\n<h3>Munir Karimjee <br />\n(Tanzania) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Rajasthan Tour Plan </h4>\n<p>Delhi – Agra – Fathepur Sikri – Bharatpur – Jaipur – Udaipur – Ranakpur – Kumbhalgarh – Mount Abu – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(09 Nights - 10 Days)</p>\n<p>\"This is a short note on our return to the UK to thank you and your company for the splendid time we spent in Rajasthan last month. The accommodation was always outstanding, the cars were comfortable and the drivers and guides at all times helpful, courteous and well informed. Our tour was an outstanding success. Do please pass on our thanks to Mr Mahesh Meena and\nhis colleagues in Tour Club for the efficient and flexible way in which the different elements of our holiday were brought together. From: Christine and Brian Boyden\" </p>\n<h3>Brian Boyden<br />\n(United Kingdom) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Karnataka Tour Plan </h4>\n<p>Bangalore – Shravanabelagola – Hassan – Udupi – Chitradurga – Hampi – Badami – Aihole –Pattadakal – Badami – Gokarna – Goa – Hometown <br />\n(09 Nights - 10 Days)</p>\n<p>\"I had a great time during my stay in India. Thanks to your careful planning and careful selection of the various agents that arranged my actual cars and drivers. The cell phone was invaluable due to unforeseen circumstances, I will definitely use your services again when I go to India; my next time will cover a smaller area. But this first trip was a good way to experience the many sights of India. I will also recommend your services to others\" </p>\n<h3> Brad Berquist <br />\n(USA) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>North India Rajasthan Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Agra – Jaipur – Udaipur – Manvar – Jaisalmer – Jodhpur – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(09 Nights - 10 Days)</p>\n<p>\"Dear Ashok, Wendy Gabriel and I had a wonderful time on the tour that you arranged for us. I will certainly recommend your services to my friends and colleagues and I will contact you when I plan another trip to India (possibly in a year or so)\"</p>\n<h3> David Hanna <br />\n(Canada) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>India Tour Plan </h4>\n<p>Delhi – Mumbai – Bangalore – Mysore – Ooty – Coimbatore – Delhi – Hometown <br />\n(07 Nights - 08 Days)</p>\n<p>Dear Ashok, Our trip to India was awesome. We paid the money in advance and received the services as promised. The only mishap was the trip from Delhi to Agra; this is when I had to call you. I really appreciate your actions in getting the driver changed immediately. However, we still hold our confidence in you and in future we will again seek your services for Indian tour. I hope we again receive the awesome service\" </p>\n<h3>Veena Naidu <br />\n(Australia) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>North India Nepal Tour</h4>\n<p>Delhi – Mandawa – Bikaner – Jaisalmer – Delhi – Jodhpur – Udaipur – Pushkar – Jaipur – Agra – Khajuraho – Varanasi – Kathmandu – Chitwan – Pokharan – Kathmandu – Hometown <br />\n(22 Nights- 23 Days)</p>\n<p> \"Meruka travel is excellent. Ashok is a wonderful guy. I do not hesitate to use them again and recommend every one. Agent Meruka arranged for Jaipur was especially ggggreattt!!!\" </p>\n<h3>Chullam Lee<br />\n(USA) </h3>\n</li>\n<li>\n<h4>Kerala Photography Tour</h4>\n<p>Mumbai – Cochin – Periyar – Alleppey – Kumarakom – Kovalam – Trivandrum – Mumbai – Hometown <br />\n(08 Nights - 09 Days)</p>\n<p>\"I have been asked by Meruka Tours to give a reference for their service in India. I organized a fashion photo shoot to Kerala in southern India last year, and had to arrange accommodation for models, photographers and art directors as well as transport across the region. Not only\nwere the guys at Meruka excellent at arranging everything (at very reasonable prices), but they were also on hand to recommend some outstanding locations for our shoot. They were polite, punctual and very reasonable. I had absolutely no complaints (and that's with temperamental models as well!) and would strongly recommend them to anybody planning a trip to India whether it's for business or for pleasure.\" </p>\n<h3> Giles Cundell<br />\n(United Kingdom) </h3>\n</li>\n</ul>\n\"The success of any business depends on the way it treats its customers. Relationship and services with your customers will reflect on the company's bottom line.\"\n<div"
